    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I am implementing a cache on Django for some data that otherwise takes a long time to compute.\nThe cache is configured to use the same database as a few other caches, but with a different prefix.\n\nCertain events are supposed to clear the cache I am implementing completely, but not the others caches in the same database. To my surprise using `.clear()` on the cache, also empties the other caches on the same database.\n\nIs this the intended behaviour?\nIf so, I think this should be documented.\n\nI have fixed the issue for now using `.delete_pattern(\"*\")` instead of `.clear()`, but I don't think this fits the intented behaviour of the API. I am currently composing a post to the Django forums to clarify.",
